@AGENTS.md

## Local Claude Skills

Project-specific Claude skills live in `.claude/skills/` and follow the current Claude Code project-skill layout.
They sit at the generated repository root, so from this folder they are in `../.claude/skills/`.

Keep skill boundaries orthogonal: `android-conventions` is the baseline ruleset, `android-feature-delivery` is the coordinator for cross-layer work, and the remaining skills own specialist domains.
Use `/android-feature-delivery <feature-description>` when you want the full research, planning, validation, and documentation workflow for a larger feature request.

- `android-conventions` - repository-wide Kotlin, MVVM, DI, navigation, strings, and doc-sync guardrails
- `android-build-verify` - choose the smallest sufficient Gradle compile, test, or assemble task
- `android-feature-delivery` - coordinate multi-layer feature work and pull in companion skills
- `android-contract-alignment` - own backend-facing DTO, enum, Retrofit, and service-alignment decisions
- `android-testing` - own unit-test, Compose UI test, and Hilt-aware instrumentation patterns
- `compose-design-system` - own shared Compose UI language, reusable components, and screen-pattern reuse
- `deploy-device` - build, install, and launch on a connected Android device
